1- Create ec2 instance
2- connect to ec2 server instance
3- update your system : - sudo yum update -y
4- Install curl : - sudo yum install curl -y
5- check curl version:- curl --version
6- install nodejs:- curl -fsSL https://rpm.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo bash -
7- install nodejs: - sudo yum install nodejs -y
8- check nodejs version:- node -v npm -v
9- install Nginx server:- sudo amazon-linux-extras install nginx1 -y
   sudo yum install nginx -y
10- Enable it to start automatically on boot:- sudo systemctl enable nginx
11- enable port custom TCD on instance security group:react port 5173
12- go to html directory:- cd /usr/share/nginx/html
13- give folder access which is in install react app:- chmod 777 -R my-app1
14- start react app using this command:- npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0






Give permission for folder:

if you just want to let Nginx or Apache serve your files:

For Nginx:
sudo chown -R nginx:nginx /var/www/my-app1
sudo chmod -R 755 /var/www/my-app1

For Apache:
sudo chown -R apache:apache /var/www/my-app1
sudo chmod -R 755 /var/www/my-app1


755 → full access for owner, read/execute for others

chown → changes ownership to the web server user

